    docs(readme): README-23 — generate/cascade examples match observed output
    
    Corrected the "Run a Mini Cascade" CLI examples against a live run in a clean
    worktree (npm install, then npm run build):
    
      ./bin/speclang generate specs/examples.spec.dir/hello-world.spec.md --dry-run
      -> exit 0; Mode: DRY RUN; Files written: 0; Would generate:
         src/generated/hello-world.spec-hello-function.ts; nothing created on disk.
    
      ./bin/speclang generate specs/examples.spec.dir/hello-world.spec.md
      -> exit 0; Mode: LIVE; Files written: 1;
         src/generated/hello-world.spec-hello-function.ts.
    
      ./bin/speclang generate ... --output-dir /tmp/... -> writes there instead (exit 0).
    
      ./bin/speclang cascade specs/examples.spec.dir/hello-world.spec.md
      -> exit 0; "Cascade complete / Generated: 1 files / Converged: Yes";
         find specs/generated -> specs/generated/hello/function.ts (1 file).
         Prints that path ABSOLUTE, not relative.
    
    What changed, all inside the generate/cascade example region:
    
    - Documented the build prerequisite: `generate` runs from bin/, `cascade` loads
      the compiled engine, so an unbuilt clone (npm install only) exits 1 with
      "SpecLang not built. Run: npm run build" — verified in this worktree before
      building.
    - The dry-run example now states it writes nothing and shows the observed
      `Mode: DRY RUN / Files written: 0` pair, plus the same command without
      --dry-run writing 1 file.
    - The cascade output line is annotated as an absolute path under the repo root.
    - Output-locations block: the per-spec sub-path comes from the block id
      (`@block::hello/function` -> hello/function.ts), verified by probing a spec at
      specs/deep/nested/bar.spec.md -> specs/deep/generated/bar/function.ts; and both
      output trees are gitignored (`generated/` in .gitignore), so running the
      examples leaves `git status` clean.
    
    The rest of the row's premise was already correct at this tip: the README showed
    specs/generated/hello/function.ts for cascade and src/generated/... for generate,
    `cascade` has no --dry-run flag (checked with cascade --help), and no
    "dry-run by default" wording survives anywhere in README/docs.
    
    Gates: npx vitest run tests/npm12-remedy-doc.test.ts -> 5 passed (the only
    README-content test). No test pins this region. Generated trees moved out of the
    worktree; commit touches README.md only.
    
